From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nikolajs Agafonovs <nikolajs.agafonovs@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 21:58:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] CSS fonts: font-family through fontconfig, font-size in
 pixels, FreeType default faces

With FreeType, links drew its normal, bold, monospaced and italic text
with the font files named in the options and fell back to the built-in
bitmaps (one serif face, no italic, no sans-serif) when they were empty;
CSS font-family and font-size were ignored, so every page came out in the
same serif at links' seven sizes.

- fontconf.c: fontconfig_font_file() asks fontconfig for the file of a
  CSS family list (in order, with the CSS generic names fontconfig lacks
  mapped), bold and/or italic, and keeps the answers for the run.
- freetype.c: a face left empty in the options is fontconfig's "serif"
  or "monospace" (in the four weights and slants) instead of the bitmap;
  faces loaded by path are loaded once and kept until freetype_done(),
  since g_clone_style() shares the face of a style (freeing it with one
  style left the clones with a freed face).
- the text format's fontface (copied and compared since long, never set)
  now carries the CSS family list; get_style_by_ta() draws with the file
  fontconfig picks for it, except fixed-width text (form controls, <pre>,
  monospace), which keeps the monospaced face their widths are counted in.
- fontpx: a size in pixels next to the 1-7 fontsize; CSS font-size (px,
  pt, pc, em, rem, %, ex, the keywords, smaller/larger) sets it, scaled by
  the user's font size against the 16 pixels browsers start from, so the
  font size setting still zooms; HTML sizes (headings, <font size>, sub,
  sup, form controls) clear it.  The font shorthand sets style, weight,
  size and family.
